1. Rust dependency closure (toktier._native)
--------------------------------------------

The compiled extension module toktier/_native.abi3.so contains the native HF
reference, corrected Gigatoken core, router, persistent store, and CUDA Driver
host. The exact package/version roster and SPDX expression for every activated
normal dependency is generated from Cargo.lock into
packaging/fast_cpu/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES-gigatoken.txt. The walk starts at
crates/toktier-py and follows every target, so target-gated crates and
procedural macros remain in the accounting record even when they are not
linked into the Linux x86-64 binary. This conservative rule prevents a linked
crate from being omitted by a target-filtering mistake.

The same closure and its dependency edges are recorded in
packaging/fast_cpu/gigatoken.cyclonedx.json. Both files are mechanically
reproduced by tools/generate_native_legal.py and checked in CI. The historical
filenames are retained as stable wheel paths; their contents describe the
whole integrated toktier._native extension, not a second Gigatoken module.

For this binary distribution, crates offered under MIT OR Apache-2.0 may be
redistributed under Apache-2.0. This selection does not alter or narrow the
upstream license choice: upstream source remains available under either
option. Copyright notices and all license/notice files found in the published
crate archives are retained in the generated bundle.

SQLite: libsqlite3-sys is built with its "bundled" feature, so the
SQLite library shipped inside that crate is compiled into the extension
module. SQLite itself is in the public domain
(https://sqlite.org/copyright.html).

The wheel carries that generated CycloneDX document in dist-info/sboms/ and
the complete deduplicated license bundle in dist-info/licenses/. The toktier
Rust crate carries the same deduplicated license bundle in its data payload
under data/packaging/fast_cpu/, alongside the crate's own dependency-closure
license bundle and SBOM under data/licenses/ and data/sbom/.


2. Generated data tables
------------------------

The GPU pre-tokenization class tables and the NFC quick-check table
(*.npy artifacts) are generated by tools/generate_class_tables.py by
probing the reference tokenizer engine (Hugging Face tokenizers) and
cross-checking against CPython's unicodedata module. The generated
tables are therefore derivatives of Unicode Character Database (UCD)
data, reached through the UCD-derived tables inside those engines. The
underlying Unicode data is subject to the Unicode License v3
(SPDX: Unicode-3.0) and the Unicode data files terms
(https://www.unicode.org/license.txt).

These table artifacts are packaged inside the current wheel and are consumed
by the certified GPU path. Per-table provenance (generator id and content
digest) is recorded in
src/toktier/kernels/tables/kernel_families.v1.json and in the support registry;
the Unicode terms reproduced below travel with the wheel.


3. Dependency-only Python packages
----------------------------------

The Python dependencies declared in pyproject.toml (tokenizers,
huggingface-hub, platformdirs, tomli, transformers, fastokens, torch,
ninja, and numpy) are install-time requirements resolved by the user's
package manager. They are not bundled into the toktier wheel, so each
installed distribution carries its own license terms. The repository also
retains Fastokens' exact Apache-2.0 and upstream notice files because its
adapter is a documented optional integration.


4. CPU fast-path acknowledgements
---------------------------------

The core toktier wheel links the corrected Gigatoken implementation into its
single private toktier._native module; it does not expose or install a second
top-level Python distribution. That engine is the default CPU full/repair path
only when its source digest, release build facts, tokenizer artifact, repair
configuration, and oracle version match the shipped certificate. Fastokens is
not bundled in the toktier wheel; the toktier project publishes a separately
installed pinned build (toktier-fastokens) for its explicit experimental
adapter, and reports what it knows about whichever Fastokens build is
installed.

