6. NVIDIA CCCL (CUB, Thrust, libcu++)
-------------------------------------

The prebuilt CUDA fatbin shipped with toktier
(src/toktier/kernels/prebuilt/pretok_kernel.fatbin; the same file travels in
the wheel and in the toktier Rust crate's data payload) contains device code
generated by template instantiation of NVIDIA CCCL 3.2.0 headers (CUB,
Thrust, and libcu++) from the CUDA 13.2 toolchain: the fatbin's device
symbols include cub DeviceSelectSweepKernel and DeviceScanKernel
instantiations with thrust counting_iterator template arguments, all in the
CCCL 3.2.0 ("_V_300200") version namespace. The JIT delivery path instead
compiles kernels on the user's machine after an explicit opt-in; those
locally built artifacts are not redistributed by this project.

Provenance of the license text reproduced below: NVIDIA/cccl repository,
tag v3.2.0 (commit 477f8bcb27eb80c28e18bbd97e5dde80ecfc648b), file LICENSE,
https://github.com/NVIDIA/cccl/blob/v3.2.0/LICENSE (retrieved file sha256
f96f51edda77fb9897de29d924d615e6bd153f4969db85fc6b7a22d7a624631e). The
header pin was cross-checked against a local CUDA 13.2 toolchain, whose
cub/version.cuh defines CUB_VERSION 300200 (CCCL 3.2.0), matching the
fatbin's version namespace.

The combined CCCL license text follows verbatim. Within it, the CUB portion
